<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>TensorParallelism on Tech Insights: AI &amp; Cloud</title><link>https://shoubhikbanerjee.github.io/blog/tags/tensorparallelism/</link><description>Recent content in TensorParallelism on Tech Insights: AI &amp; Cloud</description><generator>Hugo -- gohugo.io</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Fri, 06 Jun 2025 20:56:54 +0530</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://shoubhikbanerjee.github.io/blog/tags/tensorparallelism/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>🚀 No GPU Left Behind: How Co-located vLLM is Revolutionizing LLM Training Efficiency</title><link>https://shoubhikbanerjee.github.io/blog/p/no-gpu-left-behind-how-co-located-vllm-is-revolutionizing-llm-training-efficiency/</link><pubDate>Fri, 06 Jun 2025 20:56:54 +0530</pubDate><guid>https://shoubhikbanerjee.github.io/blog/p/no-gpu-left-behind-how-co-located-vllm-is-revolutionizing-llm-training-efficiency/</guid><description>&lt;img src="https://huggingface.co/datasets/huggingface/documentation-images/resolve/main/blog/vllm-colocate/gpus-design.png" alt="Featured image of post 🚀 No GPU Left Behind: How Co-located vLLM is Revolutionizing LLM Training Efficiency" /&gt;&lt;h1 id="-no-gpu-left-behind-how-co-located-vllm-is-revolutionizing-llm-training-efficiency"&gt;🚀 No GPU Left Behind: How Co-located vLLM is Revolutionizing LLM Training Efficiency
&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;𝗦𝘂𝗺𝗺𝗮𝗿𝘆&lt;/strong&gt;: Discover how the new co-located vLLM integration in TRL eliminates idle GPU time during GRPO training by running both training and inference on the same GPUs—delivering up to 1.73× speedup without sacrificing model quality, even on 72B parameter models.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="-the-training-bottleneck-problem"&gt;🔍 The Training Bottleneck Problem
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Training large language models using online learning methods like GRPO (introduced in the DeepSeekMath paper) requires constant generation of model outputs during the training loop. This creates a critical efficiency challenge: traditional setups force GPUs to take turns between training and inference tasks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Before TRL v0.18.0, vLLM was only supported in server mode, running as a separate process on dedicated GPUs—creating a wasteful &amp;ldquo;ping-pong&amp;rdquo; pattern:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Training GPUs run the model update step&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Training GPUs sit idle while waiting for generation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;vLLM server GPUs generate completions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;vLLM GPUs sit idle while training resumes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Repeat&amp;hellip;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This inefficient workflow results in:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;💸 Wasted GPU resources on both sides&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🔌 Increased hardware requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;⏱️ Reduced overall throughput&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;📈 Higher training costs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id="-enter-co-located-vllm-the-game-changer"&gt;🌟 Enter Co-located vLLM: The Game-Changer
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;The core innovation introduced in TRL PR #3394 is elegant yet powerful: run both training and inference on the 𝘀𝗮𝗺𝗲 GPUs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Instead of operating as a standalone server process, vLLM now runs alongside the training code within the same distributed process group. The key advantages of this colocation approach:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Unified GPU Utilization&lt;/strong&gt;: Training and inference share resources, taking turns efficiently without idle time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Direct Communication&lt;/strong&gt;: Eliminates HTTP overhead by running vLLM in-process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Seamless Scaling&lt;/strong&gt;: Works natively with torchrun for multi-node deployment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Full Parallelism Support&lt;/strong&gt;: Compatible with both Tensor and Data Parallelism&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Simplified Deployment&lt;/strong&gt;: No separate server management needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To enable this in your training pipeline, it&amp;rsquo;s as simple as changing one parameter:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;div class="chroma"&gt;
&lt;table class="lntable"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;2
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;3
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;4
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;5
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-python" data-lang="python"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;training_args&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;GRPOConfig&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;...&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;use_vllm&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;True&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;vllm_mode&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;colocate&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;# This enables colocation!&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 id="-real-world-performance-gains"&gt;📊 Real-World Performance Gains
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;The team ran extensive experiments comparing traditional server mode to the new co-located approach. The results were impressive across various model sizes and configurations:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id="-for-smaller-models-15b-parameters"&gt;🔹 For Smaller Models (1.5B parameters)
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Up to 1.43× speedup with larger batch sizes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Better performance with less tensor parallelism&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id="-for-medium-models-7b-parameters"&gt;🔹 For Medium Models (7B parameters)
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1.35× speedup at larger batch sizes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Performance improves with more tensor parallelism, reaching 1.73× speedup&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id="-for-massive-models-qwen25-math-72b"&gt;🔹 For Massive Models (Qwen2.5-Math-72B)
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Co-located setup achieves ~1.26× faster throughput even with 𝙛𝙚𝙬𝙚𝙧 GPUs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Equal model quality on Math500 benchmark compared to traditional training&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;One crucial innovation that enables efficient training of massive models is the integration of vLLM&amp;rsquo;s &lt;code&gt;sleep()&lt;/code&gt; API into the training loop. This function temporarily frees GPU memory, allowing:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Level 1 Sleep&lt;/strong&gt;: Unloads model weights but keeps them accessible in CPU memory&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Level 2 Sleep&lt;/strong&gt;: Completely unloads both weights and KV cache&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For GRPO, which updates the model after every step, Level 2 sleep provides maximum memory efficiency, avoiding contention between training and generation tasks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="-technical-implementation-details"&gt;📈 Technical Implementation Details
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;The implementation combines several advanced techniques to maximize performance:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Process Group Awareness&lt;/strong&gt;: Co-located vLLM respects the torch.distributed process group:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;div class="chroma"&gt;
&lt;table class="lntable"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;2
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;3
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;4
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;5
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;6
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;7
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;8
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;9
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-python" data-lang="python"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="bp"&gt;self&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;vllm_tensor_parallel_size&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="bp"&gt;self&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;tp_group&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;_&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;torch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;distributed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;new_subgroups_by_enumeration&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;list&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;range&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;i&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="bp"&gt;self&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;vllm_tensor_parallel_size&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;i&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="bp"&gt;self&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;vllm_tensor_parallel_size&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;))&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;i&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="ow"&gt;in&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;range&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="bp"&gt;self&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;accelerator&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;num_processes&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;//&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="bp"&gt;self&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;vllm_tensor_parallel_size&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;ol start="2"&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Memory Management&lt;/strong&gt;: For large models like Qwen2.5-72B, DeepSpeed ZeRO Stage 3 optimizations handle memory constraints:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Offloading optimizer states to CPU&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Overlapping communication with computation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Using contiguous gradients to reduce memory fragmentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accelerate Integration&lt;/strong&gt;: The whole system leverages HuggingFace&amp;rsquo;s Accelerate library for streamlined distributed training.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;h2 id="-the-future-of-efficient-llm-training"&gt;🔮 The Future of Efficient LLM Training
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Despite a few challenges like occasional segmentation faults during shutdown (reported in Issue #16993), the co-located vLLM approach represents a significant advancement in LLM training efficiency.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The most important lessons from this work:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🔥 Co-located inference dramatically improves GPU utilization without requiring additional hardware&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🧠 Memory management via vLLM&amp;rsquo;s sleep() is crucial for large-scale training&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;⚡ The approach maintains model quality while delivering substantial throughput gains&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This innovation makes training large models faster, cheaper, and more accessible—especially important as models continue to grow in size and complexity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="-try-it-yourself"&gt;💡 Try It Yourself
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Want to experience the efficiency gains firsthand? Here&amp;rsquo;s a minimal example to get started with GRPO training using co-located vLLM:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;div class="chroma"&gt;
&lt;table class="lntable"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt; 1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt; 2
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt; 3
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt; 4
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt; 5
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt; 6
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt; 7
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt; 8
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt; 9
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;10
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;11
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;12
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;13
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;14
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;15
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;16
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;17
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;18
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;19
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;20
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;21
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;22
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;23
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;24
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;25
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;26
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-python" data-lang="python"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="kn"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nn"&gt;datasets&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;load_dataset&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="kn"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nn"&gt;trl&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;GRPOConfig&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;GRPOTrainer&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;dataset&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;load_dataset&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;trl-lib/tldr&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;split&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;train&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;def&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;reward_len&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;completions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;**&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;kwargs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;):&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;abs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;20&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;len&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;completion&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;))&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;completion&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="ow"&gt;in&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;completions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;training_args&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;GRPOConfig&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;output_dir&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;Qwen2-0.5B-GRPO&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;use_vllm&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;True&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;vllm_mode&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;colocate&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;# Enable colocation&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;vllm_gpu_memory_utilization&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mf"&gt;0.3&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
